      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO VOICE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Active voice emphasizes the doer of the action, whereas passive voice emphasizes the receiver.",
        "Voice conversion involves swapping the Subject and Object, always utilizing the third form of the verb (V3).",
        "Tense-wise voice conversion forms the core framework for competitive English grammar questions.",
        "Intransitive verbs cannot be transformed into passive voice because they lack a direct object.",
        "Imperative, interrogative, negative, and modal verb structures follow specialized rules during voice transformation."
      ],
      "id": "zsx2i9g"
    },
